  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nCurrently browsers behave differently when `window.requestAnimationFrame()` is called for an iframe that is actually hidden via `display: none`. In Firefox the callback is never called because no rendering is done, but in both Chrome and Safari I can see that `requestAnimationFrame` is repeatedly executed.\n\nHere the example HTML that I'm using:\n\n```\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <body>\n    <iframe style=\"display:none\" srcdoc='\n      <script>\n        function tick() {\n          console.log(\"requestAnimationFrame fired in iframe\");\n          window.requestAnimationFrame(tick);\n        }\n        window.requestAnimationFrame(tick);\n      </script>\n    '>\n    </iframe>\n    </body>\n</html>\n```",
